{"book":6,"chapter":9,"context":{"chapter":9,"title":"The Gibeonite Deception","summary":"The people of Gibeon pretend to come from a distant country, with worn-out sacks, patched wineskins and dry, moldy bread. Israel's leaders make a treaty without asking the Lord, discover the trick three days later, but keep their oath.","background":"Deuteronomy 20 allowed peace terms with distant cities but not with the cities of Canaan, which explains the disguise. Gibeon was a large town a few miles northwest of Jerusalem (10:2). Generations later, Saul broke this oath by killing Gibeonites, and Israel suffered famine for it (2 Samuel 21:1-2).","customs":[{"term":"Wine bottles","verses":"9:4","note":"Wine was carried in goatskin bags. Old skins dried out, cracked, and had to be patched, so torn, mended skins suggested a very long journey."},{"term":"Hewers of wood and drawers of water","verses":"9:21-27","note":"The lowest kinds of manual labor. The Gibeonites were assigned to serve the congregation and the altar."}],"watchFor":["'And asked not counsel at the mouth of the Lord' (v. 14).","An oath sworn in the Lord's name is binding even though it was won by deceit (vv. 18–20)."],"connections":["Deuteronomy 20:10-15","Deuteronomy 29:11","2 Samuel 21:1-2"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיְהִי","vayhi","H1961","Hc/Vqw3ms","and it was"],["כִשְׁמֹעַ","khishmoa'","H8085","HR/Vqcc","when heard"],["כָּל","kal-","H3605","HNcmsc","all"],["הַמְּלָכִים","hamelakhim","H4428","HTd/Ncmpa","the kings"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","who"],["בְּעֵבֶר","be'ever","H5676","HR/Ncmsc","[were] on [the] other side of"],["הַיַּרְדֵּן","haiyarden","H3383","HTd/Npl","the Jordan"],["בָּהָר","bahar","H2022","HRd/Ncmsa","in the hill country"],["וּבַשְּׁפֵלָה","uvashefelah","H8219","HC/Rd/Ncfsa","and in the Shephelah"],["וּבְכֹל","uvekhol","H3605","HC/R/Ncmsc","and in all"],["חוֹף","chof","H2348","HNcmsc","[the] coast of"],["הַיָּם","haiyam","H3220","HTd/Ncmsa","the sea"],["הַגָּדוֹל","hagadol","H1419","HTd/A